@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 100
title QR attendance check-in
autonumber
participant "Student" as U
participant "Scanner page / AttendanceCubit" as UI
participant "Camera / location adapter" as H
participant "CheckInWithQrToken use case" as D
participant "AttendanceRepositoryImpl / remote data source" as R
participant "Firebase callable function" as C
participant "Cloud Firestore" as F
note over U, F: Precondition: authenticated student; professor opened a session and displays a server-signed rotating QR token.
U -> UI: Open scanner and scan QR
UI -> H: Request camera and location permission; explain purpose
alt Permission denied or location unavailable
H --> UI: Permission / location failure
UI -> U: Explain how to retry; do not submit check-in
else QR scanned and location available
H --> UI: sessionId, signed token, current coordinates
UI -> D: Check in; show submitting state
D -> R: checkInWithQrToken(sessionId, token, location)
R -> C: Callable request with Firebase Auth context
C -> C: Require authenticated student; derive uid from auth
group Server transaction: validation and record creation
C -> F: Read session, lecture, user, enrolment and existing record
F --> C: Authoritative state
C -> C: Check open session, enrolment, signed token + expiry, geofence
alt Invalid token / closed session / wrong course / outside area
C --> R: Typed rejection; no attendance write
else Valid request; record already exists
C --> R: Return existing record; do not overwrite corrections
else Valid request; no record exists
C -> F: Create attendance_records/{sessionId}_{uid}; server timestamp
F --> C: Transaction committed
C --> R: Attendance record
end
end
R --> D: Success(AttendanceRecord) or Failure(AppFailure)
D --> UI: Result; clear submitting state
UI -> U: Confirm course / lecture, or show actionable error
end
note over U, F: Online confirmation required. Network failures are retryable; deterministic record IDs prevent duplicate attendance.
note over U, F: Signing secrets stay server-side. GPS is client-reported evidence, not proof against location spoofing.
@enduml
